cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this explainer or its cards, please cite it as below. The DOI is that of the gallery (concept DOI, all versions); the version DOI of the gallery release that adds this station is filled in when it is published."
title: "Co-reading explainer: moy-1, received version v3.1 — an audited figure of how OLMo-3 32B answers one two-circle problem when a single sentence blocks the easy answer, and what the house tested after the figure"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Higashida
    given-names: Manabu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7393-2957"
    affiliation: "D3 Center, The University of Osaka, Osaka, Japan"
version: "3.1"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23992312
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/moyhig-ecs/coread-explainer-gallery"
abstract: >-
  An interactive isometric figure (43 states in 15 chapters; ja / en; dark / light; also an anywidget for Jupyter / marimo), 1920×1080
  stills, a two-voice script and a ledger of what can and cannot be said, built from the frozen outputs of pre-registered measurements on
  the moy-1 problem (OLMo-3 32B base and Think; the open and blocked question texts), followed by the 20 cards the house froze after the
  first figure (olm76–olm128). The frozen files the figure reads are copied into data/ (192 files) and the cards (PREREG = the frozen
  promise, RESULT = the read-out, corrections appended) into cards/ verbatim (Japanese), with an English index. Every number on the page
  is anchored to the data (check_claims.py, 689 anchors). The question texts are traced with md5 to the frozen configuration and to the
  literals of the public ConstructGap suite (tag v1.0.1).
keywords:
